    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug. The issue was in **packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts** where the `gate` command handler was only passing positional arguments to the spawned `frai-gate` CLI, missing the flags like `--ci`.\n\n**The Problem:**\nWhen Commander.js parses `frai gate init --ci`, it separates positional arguments from flags. The action handler was only receiving the positional args in its parameter, so `--ci` was lost.\n\n**The Fix:**\nChanged the action handler to use `process.argv` to capture all raw command-line arguments after the 'gate' command, ensuring flags are preserved:\n\n```typescript\n// Before: args parameter only contained positional arguments\n.action(async (args: string[]) => {\n  const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateCli, ...(args ?? [])], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n})\n\n// After: extract all arguments including flags from process.argv\n.action(async () => {\n  const gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\n  const gateArgs = gateIndex >= 0 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : [];\n  const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateCli, ...gateArgs], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n})\n```\n\n**Verification:**\n\u2705 Rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n\u2705 Tested `frai gate init --ci` in a clean directory\n\u2705 Both FRAI-SPEC.md and .github/workflows/rai-gate.yml were created successfully",
